> - **The same defect, where the PR didn't look.** When the change fixes a kind of defect (an unguarded input, a missing null check), look for the same kind on the same path in the code it left alone, such as every other input that reaches the line the PR now protects. Lines the PR moves or rewrites are its own code, so read them as new code, such as for a null that throws or a stream an error path leaves open: a probe that reports only differences from the base misses a defect both carry. An instance that predates the PR blocks only if it defeats the PR's own guarantee; otherwise it is a suggestion, which the author may take as a follow-up.
